{"id": "EUVD-2026-64542", "enisaUuid": "0bb8d8bf-b0ac-3524-af08-6d00b9ff563b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neventfs: Use children field for rcu head and add memory barriers\n\nWhen an eventfs inode is freed, it sets ei->is_freed and then uses its\nei->list to add it to the srcu link list as the list field is a union with\nthe rcu list head. As the ei->list is used to iterate over an SRCU\nprotected list without taking the eventfs_mutex, there's nothing stopping\nthe iteration over that list to see the ei->rcu instead of the ei->list\nand it will read a corrupt target.\n\nTo fix this, change the union of the rcu list head with the children list.\nOn freeing the eventfs inode, set the is_free and execute a smp_wmb()\nbefore adding the eventfs inode to the SRCU list.\n\nOn iteration of the ei->children list, at the start, execute a smp_rmb()\nand then read the is_freed of the ei to see if the children list is still\nvalid. If is_freed is set, then the ei_child read is not valid and the\nloop should exit immediately.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:31:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:03", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25d27d5fa8645ab61018c3efec5c69f49280ca7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b95382da85cff3bf0f922ff0275f186abdadfce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b80707b9e27671e10840d17c6f8f774c4ad9847", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/004f7232e49730448f91665e76bdd7dff8e0c638", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0ece16ffca7384787b692431961ce202907acf5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c64v-3vw2-pvwh", "CVE-2026-74605"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11bde379-cdf5-3fdf-9110-a58d31a041c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "177ca2b4-cae2-38db-adee-dbb568966d78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "29e1f0e6-3566-3ff8-b4d5-14d3b6918297", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "305c4e4d80aca2c2d9cf2ebdea56e2eca6d3a6aa"}, {"id": "35aa3770-a752-319a-9b38-1ee52726c0b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "6ba52795-b95c-320c-a5c9-e9db21995a81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "704f960dbee2f1634f4b4e16f208cb16eaf41c1e <2b80707b9e27671e10840d17c6f8f774c4ad9847"}, {"id": "6f54e338-0e7f-3021-a0e0-1bd61a4a4752", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7.6 <6.8"}, {"id": "6faf9d2e-88a8-3c54-a9e0-56dbfec24910", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "73bbebf2-0aac-3628-a910-7f438013aaca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.18 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "77db145e-aa59-3d9c-84f9-bfbd7f150096", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "819a1081-5e15-3ee1-8139-9827228e8b7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f3f41f444b321ec393edbc251e024fd62658ce55 <25d27d5fa8645ab61018c3efec5c69f49280ca7d"}, {"id": "966234bd-9a81-329f-8d61-a283361b3e16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "704f960dbee2f1634f4b4e16f208cb16eaf41c1e <1b95382da85cff3bf0f922ff0275f186abdadfce"}, {"id": "9b7ce471-8043-331a-b4e7-a90647d7012f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "aedc244b-6f91-3736-a8f4-40e03153d97b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "b1b89287-5bf7-36cd-a742-66cabe0d4723", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "704f960dbee2f1